e, statement II is true.\n\n- The domain excludes exactly the integer multiples of $\\pi$. The number $\\frac{-13\\pi }{2}$ is not an integer multiple of $\\pi$. Hence, statement III is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517056 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326" :knowledge-point/title "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a99b2373-abce-568f-9b15-c1bb8f7ab1d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517060} {:answer/id #uuid "f79dd989-4971-5762-a2ba-202aa01c4158" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a99b2373-abce-568f-9b15-c1bb8f7ab1d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517060} :answer-field/id #uuid "111a4744-b4c9-52fa-b0f8-83e1d0b3e24d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516993} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10e2d8b0-2537-5969-b8e5-2a6df09d26a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516992} {:answer/id #uuid "3a79479a-747f-50cf-a296-e83d33924672" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10e2d8b0-2537-5969-b8e5-2a6df09d26a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516992} :answer-field/id #uuid "4eca9804-f62b-550c-b7f1-d0b58439e892" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517025} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0afb53c5-3b32-5ccc-8fac-090d7fafef4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516991} {:answer/id #uuid "735275b4-c368-5115-9296-2ea255b21907" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "735275b4-c368-5115-9296-2ea255b21907" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517041} :answer-field/id #uuid "d79e92c9-1bd6-5e55-a4dc-9bd82ddf2a09" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517078}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "98d10a33-9e93-5824-8112-36ddfc7272c5" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\csc x$?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The domain is all real numbers except integer multiples of $\\pi$.\n- **II.** The range is $(-\\infty,-1]\\cup[1,\\infty)$.\n- **III.** The graph has a zero at $x=0$." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\csc x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The function's domain is all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi$. Hence, statement I is true.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty,-1]\\cup[1,\\infty)$.  Hence, statement II is true.\n\n- The cosecant graph does not intersect the $x$-axis. Hence, statement III is false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517062 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326" :knowledge-point/title "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58cf80cc-ab53-5783-bcc2-db059f3f00b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517030} {:answer/id #uuid "b139766e-16ba-5da1-81f4-45b69bcf78f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517063}] :